      "defect": "A shared bucket tagged with a tenant-prefix scheme has an app-signer identity that either allows path traversal (allow_traversal=true) or disables prefix enforcement (enforce_prefix=false). The signer can mint presigned URLs that escape the tenant prefix — either by including \"../\" in the signed key or by omitting the prefix entirely.\n",
      "infection": "Any tenant using this app-signer can request a presigned URL targeting another tenant's prefix. The URL is validly signed, so the bucket policy's signature-based tenant gate never triggers — S3 honors the URL exactly as the signer minted it. This is architecturally invisible to the bucket itself: the ACL remains private, the bucket policy remains tenant-aware, but the signer's presigned URLs bypass both layers. Cross-tenant read or write happens at signing time, not at S3's request-evaluation time. In the unikrn-254200 pattern, the signer gives tenant A's session a URL that lists or overwrites tenant B's objects — no S3-layer misconfiguration to audit.\n",
      "failure": "Cross-tenant data breach and data integrity failure. Tenant A reads, overwrites, or deletes tenant B's objects through presigned URLs the application legitimately issued. Audit logs show tenant A making signed requests against the bucket — which is normal behavior — so detection requires cross-referencing signer identity state against per-request prefixes, a correlation few shops build. Remediation requires fixing every app-signer with the unsafe setting and revoking any outstanding presigned URLs.\n",
      "delta": [
        {
          "property_label": "tags tenant mode",
          "property_path": "storage.tags.tenant_mode",
          "current_value": "shared",
          "fix_action": "change from \"shared\" to any other value, or remove"
        },
        {
          "property_label": "tags tenant prefix",
          "property_path": "storage.tags.tenant_prefix",
          "current_value": "users/{user_id}/{date}/",
          "fix_action": "remove this property from the configuration"
        }
      ]
    }
